{
  "requirement": "HC MUST use one {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.validator` per assessment. Its usage record MUST report that validator’s attempt and token totals under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.Validator.usage` and its failure and retry counts under {cite}`requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`. The record MUST distinguish partial or unavailable token measurements from complete totals and preserve the available cache and reasoning breakdowns. The assessment MUST also report elapsed time and tool-call counts by tool.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.authoring.usage_requests`**\n1. One validator is used per assessment.\n2. The usage record reports the validator's attempt and token totals (`Validator.usage`).\n3. The record reports the validator's failure and retry counts (`usage_requests.failures`).\n4. The record distinguishes partial or unavailable token measurements from complete totals.\n5. The record preserves the available cache and reasoning breakdowns.\n6. The assessment reports elapsed time.\n7. The assessment reports tool-call counts by tool.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Validator totals, failures and retries.**\n  - `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt]` runs five 429 failures followed by one success.\n  - It asserts `provider_usage` for `attempts` (6), `retries` (5) and `failed_attempts` (5). The failures were recovered by a retry, as the failures clause requires.\n  - It asserts every token category as `{reported, missing_attempts}`: input 100/5, output 15/5, cached 20/5, cache_creation 0/6 and reasoning 0/5.\n  - That covers the validator totals, partial and unavailable measurements, and the cache and reasoning breakdowns.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#impl[AssessmentUsage<'_,%20'_>/Drop]/fn[drop]` copies `validator.usage()` into `provider_usage`, and this test confirms that path.\n  - `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` and `success_resets_backoff_and_retries_keep_history_without_repeating_tools` cover request counts and outcomes over abandoned and retried requests. `failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt` covers the failure record and its `retried` flag.\n- **Complete versus partial or unavailable tokens.**\n  - `src/authoring/usage.rs#mod[tests]/fn[token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown]` asserts that `tokens.complete` is false while a request is in flight and true once all requests are measured. It asserts false again after an unmeasured failed request.\n  - It also checks that the cache, cache-creation and reasoning sums stay separate and that missing counters are null.\n  - `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` checks that an optional counter measured in only some requests stays complete=false, and that absent counters stay null.\n  - `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` checks incomplete totals on cancellation.\n- **Cache and reasoning breakdowns end to end.**\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[claude_requests_carry_cache_checkpoints_and_record_cache_usage]` asserts per-request and total cached and cache-creation tokens.\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[openai_responses_replays_tool_calls_and_records_usage]` asserts the cached (6) and reasoning (4) totals.\n  - The Ollama and Bedrock CLI tests assert the input and output totals and `complete`.\n- **Elapsed time.** `completed_requests_and_the_run_record_elapsed_time` asserts the exact per-request elapsed value and that the run elapsed time covers the elapsed time of the request. `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` checks that an elapsed value is kept for a cancelled request.\n- **Tool-call counts by tool.** `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` asserts per-tool `tool_calls`, `tool_failures` and `tool_skipped`. The CLI tests (`ollama_cli_…`, `explicit_ignored_reads_…`, `bedrock_cli_…`) assert per-tool counts in real runs.\n- **One validator per assessment.**\n  - No test asserts it directly.\n  - It is structural: `src/authoring/sdk.rs#fn[run]` constructs a single `Validator::new` and wraps it in `AssessmentUsage`.\n  - A violation, such as a validator recreated on retry, would drop earlier counts. The throttled test's exact totals (6 attempts and 5 retries) would catch that.\n\n**Cited requirement and context**\n- The `Validator.usage` and `usage_requests.failures` obligations are applied in the subject's case by the throttled test, as above.\n- I did not reassess the cited requirements' own tests. Terminal-failure retention belongs to the `usage_requests.failures` review.\n\nI found no established gap, and the acknowledgments list is empty.",
  "references": "690ccd5d774a163bfa61c7627bb1240393187d61c644988217fdf8ac050a5d06",
