      "text": [
        ":::{req} usage_requests",
        "HC MUST use one {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.validator` per assessment. Its usage record MUST report that validator’s attempt and token totals under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.Validator.usage` and its failure and retry counts under {cite}`requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`. The record MUST distinguish partial or unavailable token measurements from complete totals and preserve the available cache and reasoning breakdowns. The assessment MUST also report elapsed time and tool-call counts by tool.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.Validator.usage",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.Validator.usage"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} Validator.usage",
        "",
        "`usage()` returns the validator’s cumulative usage. Every agent call contributes its usage to the execution that invoked it, including calls that return an error. The validator adds that usage before `verify` or `refresh_evidence` returns, including on `Err`. Reusing current evidence adds no usage. Loading, checking, and storing evidence also leave the counters unchanged.",
        "",
        "For totals across validators that share a domain cache, see {cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.usage`.",
        "",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "impl<'d, D: Domain> Validator<'d, D> {",
        "    pub fn usage(&self) -> &UsageStats;",
        "}",
        "```",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} usage_requests.failures",
        "Each assessment’s usage record MUST include its total failed provider attempts and retries, including failures recovered by a successful retry. A terminal failure MUST retain the accumulated counts.",
        ":::"
      ]
